  "nl_text": "The rschema_0025 database is used to store information about tobacco products, departments, employees, production records, and production record details. The tobacco products table contains information about the products, including their ID, name, type, production date, shelf life, sales price, and production batch number. The department table contains information about the departments, including their ID, name, total number of people in the department, person in charge ID, and department responsibilities. The employee table contains information about the employees, including their ID, name, gender, phone, position, joining date, and department ID. The production record table contains information about the sales records, including the product ID, sales time, salesperson ID, customer name, sales quantity, sales price, customer phone, customer address, and sales type. The production record details table contains information about the production record details, including the production record ID, producer ID, and production record ID. The database also has foreign key constraints to ensure referential integrity, with the employee table referencing the department table, the production record table referencing the tobacco products table and the employee table, and the production record details table referencing the production record table and the employee table.",
  "gold_question": "The tobacco product enterprise management system needs to comprehensively manage the company's tobacco products from production, inventory, sales and other aspects. The system should support functions such as detailed records of tobacco products, sales tracking, and production process monitoring, and be able to generate various reports to help management make scientific decisions. At the same time, the system should also have the functions of department collaboration, employee management, and department performance appraisal to improve the overall operational efficiency of the enterprise. Tobacco has information such as name, type, production date, shelf life, price, and production batch number. Multiple departments of the enterprise collaborate, and each department has a department name, person in charge, and contact information. Employee management includes employee number, name, gender, telephone number, and position. Each time production is carried out, the products, quantity, producer, and production time produced must be recorded. When selling, the products, quantity, salesperson, customer, and sales time sold must be recorded.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0025.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0025\nCREATE TABLE `tobacco_products` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `production_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `shelf_life` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `sales_price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `production_batch_number` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `departments` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `total_people` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `person_in_charge_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `responsibilities` text NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `departments_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`person_in_charge_id`) REFERENCES `employees` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `employees` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `gender` char(1) NOT NULL,\n  `phone` varchar(15) NOT NULL,\n  `position` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `joining_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `department_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `employees_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`department_id`) REFERENCES `departments` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `production_records` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `sales_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `salesperson_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `customer_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `sales_quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `sales_price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `customer_phone` varchar(15) NOT NULL,\n  `customer_address` text NOT NULL,\n  `sales_type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `production_records_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`product_id`) REFERENCES `tobacco_products` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `production_records_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`salesperson_id`) REFERENCES `employees` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `production_record_details` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `producer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `production_record_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `production_record_details_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`production_record_id`) REFERENCES `production_records` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `production_record_details_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`producer_id`) REFERENCES `employees` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
